ing each substep of execution. This expression will be highlighted.\n\n\nAnalyzing available data structures to extract and highlight specific code snippets within the editor. Focusing on `step` and `currentSubstep` properties. Properties like `codeSnippet`, `a\n<truncated 642 bytes>\nn strings, then handling various assignment and conditional statements.\n\nThe first strategy is to use the `rawLine` and check for matching substrings. It's likely that a more targeted approach is needed for certain assignment types, for example, handling augmented assignments and conditions. The code structure for these assignments shows `step.operationDetail` is key.\n\nConditional expressions require special handling via the `step.condition` property, checking `cond.expr` and `cond.leftExpr`. Augmented and standard assignments require identifying the `op.rhsExpr` and `op.target`. I need to ensure that the logic is correct for all these cases.\n\n\nAnalyzing different event types and corresponding code structures will provide targeted highlighting expressions.  Loop iterations will highlight loop variables or conditional expressions. Function returns will highlight either the returned value or the \"return\" keyword.\n\nFunction calls will highlight the entire function call expression, including the name and arguments, or just the name. Function and class definitions will highlight the name. Default highlighting will check if the current substep's code snippet matches any part of the line.\n\n\nAnalyzing rendering with `activeFocusSnippet`, the highlighted snippet should be wrapped in a Thonny-style box within the active line. The box requires a dark border, a light background, and maintains syntax highlighting. I need to determine how to wrap the snippet and apply relevant CSS classes.\nThe highlight box will reside inside of the `<span class=\"thonny-token-box\">`. I need to ensure syntax highlighting is preserved. Further, I will evaluate the implementation details in Area 2.\n\n\nAnalyzing the provided examples reveals the exact token-level highlighting mechanism. The objective now is to apply this precise highlighting strategy, using the `.thonny-token-box`, in conjunction with the identified expression extraction logic. This will ensure synchronized highlighting in both code areas, replicating the target visual behavior.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"\"C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/code-flow-visualizer/app_build/styles.css\"","EndLine":"670","StartLine":"620","toolAction":"\"Viewing teach-code-box in styles.css\"","toolSummary":"\"Check teach-code-box styles in styles.css\""}}],"truncated_fields":["thinking"]}
